{
  "info": {
    "name": "Order Management - Steps 1 to 8",
    "_postman_id": "5a8249a7-2887-4df8-8c55-e7ad5a3abce5",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "# Steps 1-8 collection\nUse this with order-management-steps-1-to-8.zip, not the original Java 17 implementation.\n\nImport the JSON as a collection into Postman Desktop. No environment file is needed. Avoid environment variables with the same names as collection variables. All URLs use localhost ports 8081/8082.\n\nNormal verification: start Docker stack; leave testMode=normal; run folders 01, 02, 03 in order. Running the entire collection in normal mode skips manual folders. productId/orderId are captured automatically. Run once per newly created product. Test Results contains assertions; polling tests may perform subsequent GETs after the original response.\n\nManual outage: stop RabbitMQ in your terminal; change testMode to outage; run folder 04. Inspect DB and logs as described. Manual recovery: start RabbitMQ; wait for broker health and the 15-second breaker interval; change testMode to recovery; run folder 05. Restore normal mode after testing. This collection never stops/starts containers by itself.\n\nExpected API: POST /products 201; GET /products and /products/{id} 200; POST /orders 201/PENDING or 503 with error/orderId. Product validation/not-found have code/message JSON. Order validation returns the default Spring error format. There is no idempotency header support, reservation status endpoint, GET /orders, DLQ or response message in this version. Repeated POST orders create new orders. Do not reuse older collection tests for those features.\n\nDatabase check: docker compose exec postgres psql -U app -d orderdb -c 'SELECT id, order_id, status FROM orders ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 10;'\nConsumer logs: docker compose logs --tail=100 product-service\n\nThe JSON and JavaScript syntax have been checked; live API execution and UI import have not been verified in the preparation workspace. The automated six Mockito tests are separate from these live API checks.\n"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "noauth"
  },
